UnitPactoUsernameNFT::claim
├── when the claim is valid
│   ├── it stores the username record for the npub
│   ├── it mints the ERC-721 token to the claimer
│   └── it emits UsernameClaimed
├── when the name is already claimed
│   └── it reverts
├── when the name is reserved
│   └── it reverts
├── when the npub already has a record
│   └── it reverts
├── when the claimer address already controls a record
│   └── it reverts
├── when the mint fee is not paid
│   └── it reverts
├── when the claim signature is invalid
│   └── it reverts
├── when the nostr signature is invalid
│   └── it reverts
├── when the npub hash does not match the pubkey
│   └── it reverts
├── when the nonce is reused
│   └── it reverts
└── when the binding is expired
    └── it reverts


UnitPactoUsernameNFT::nameAvailable
├── when the name is short uppercase or has digits and hyphens
│   └── it returns true
└── when the name is reserved
    └── it returns false


UnitPactoUsernameNFT::initiateAddressTransfer
├── when called by the active controller with a valid pending address
│   ├── it sets the pending address
│   └── it emits AddressTransferInitiated
├── when called by a non-controller
│   └── it reverts
└── when a pending transfer already exists
    └── it reverts


UnitPactoUsernameNFT::claimAddressTransfer
├── when called by the pending recipient
│   ├── it swaps the active EVM address
│   ├── it transfers the ERC-721 token to the new controller
│   └── it emits AddressTransferClaimed
├── when called by a non-pending address
│   └── it reverts
└── when no pending transfer exists
    └── it reverts


UnitPactoUsernameNFT::cancelAddressTransfer
├── when called by the active controller
│   ├── it clears the pending address
│   └── it emits AddressTransferCancelled
└── when no pending transfer exists
    └── it reverts


UnitPactoUsernameNFT::transfer
└── when a standard ERC-721 transfer is attempted
    └── it reverts
